#905

## What to build

The pilot, one real lane start through the whole path. In a target's checkout the director runs `octo-feather-lane start TICKET --goal TITLE --outcome TEXT --brief-file FILE` (a new subcommand of the existing lane tool; its logic in a stdlib Python module beside it, the subcommand thin; flag names may change if `--help` says why). It:

- derives the lane key through the target's tracker skill (`lane-key`), resolved the way `octo-feather-start` resolves it (pi-role's tracker skill), and reads the ticket with `issue-view`;
- fetches origin and adds the worktree, a sibling of the checkout named `<checkout dir>-<key>`, on a new branch `<key>` from origin's main;
- starts the supervisor by running the `octo-feather-start` that sits beside the command in the same kit (`--issue TICKET --cwd WORKTREE`), unchanged: it stays the only way a supervisor starts (`octo-feather-start` is owner-gated: do not edit it);
- writes the lane record `$(octo-feather-state)/lanes/<key>.toml` from the spawn output: comms spec `#lane-record` keys (supervisor pane, repository as `gh repo view` names the checkout's repo, issue key, goal, started_at, waiting_on "");
- sends the supervisor, with `herdr-say`, first `/goal <outcome> for <key>, delivered through implement-spec; done when an owner gate is pending (review link or merge ask sent) or PR merged and lane torn down`, then the brief: a header of generated lane facts (lane key, parent issue, director pane, worktree, branch, the main commit it started from), then the file's text;
- appends one director log line (comms spec `#handoff-director-prod`: issue, note);
- prints `key=<key> pane=<pane> issue=<ticket>`.

Recipe only, never copy wholesale: the private `$(octo-feather-state)/bin/start-lane`. Its ctrl+c retry for a stalled first message is NOT carried over: herdr-spawn's readiness wait already covers a fresh pane (herdr-comms SKILL.md, Spawn an agent, #871); a failed `herdr-say` stops the command loud, naming the step.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] issue-lifecycle#acceptance-lane-start: the start command, run for an open ticket, leaves the workspace, worktree, branch, lane record, the goal then the brief, one director log line, and prints key, pane and issue
- [ ] demo: `octo-feather-lane start 905 --goal "Lane start as one command" --outcome "a scratch proof" --brief-file brief.md` run in a scratch target clone with the testkit's herdr and gh stand-ins first on PATH: prints `key=gh905 pane=... issue=905`, and the record, the stand-in's prompt log and the director log show the lane

## Seams

Seam: issue-lifecycle#acceptance-lane-start: `octo-feather-lane start` run as a command, the testkit's herdr and gh stand-ins on PATH, the real octo-feather-start and herdr-spawn behind it

Skills: python, herdr-comms

